        <p>JS MARRIAGE A FAILURE?</p>
        <p>What a question to ask, but how often could it be answered in the affirmative, the principal cause being the improvidence of Furnishing on the Hire System. Since (err advertisements have appeared pointing out the disadveuta.ges we have re- ceived several '&lt;eters egreeing with our denunciations of this- pernicious sys'em. Each Hire Agreement specifies that after- the deposit is paid, so many weekly payments shall be made and that until the whole of the sum mentioned is paid the goods shall not become the property of the would-be pur- chaser, and that if any of the payments are neglected to the exact time specified the goods may be forcibly taken away and the whole of the payments forfeited. County Court judges have denounced the sy tern, inasmuch as the vendor gets both money and goods. Again, the pri .es charged are enormous, without ally respect being paid to the quality, in many cases being worn out before they are paid for. To com- bat this system, and open the eyes ot the public, Worsley's of " The Pantheon," Gayt horn, Manchester, the Largest Retailer* of Second-hand Furniture in the world, have determined to- allow all respectable householders to have furniture at the- ticketed marked cash price, a small percentage being charged. for the converrence of payment by the week, month, or quarter. On the fourth page of the "Examiner" we advertise a list of Bargains every week, any of which can be had and paid for by convenient intervals, the articles being delivered upon the first payment being made. Furniture from £5 to £1 GO3 may be arranged for in this way. To give an idea of the equity of cur proposals we are prepared to supply for a working man a House of Furniture complete,, thoroughly good and sabstantiel (every article warranted). price £2O cash down, not a penny less, or 10 jer cent extra if credit is given, making £22. Full particulars sent on application.</p>
        <p>GREAT BARGAINS AT WORSLEY'S. ONE HUNDRED BEDROOM SUITES ON VIEW. The Marvel : This is a solid American walnut Bedroom- Suite, beautifully finished, has en excellent Wardrobe. with plate-glass centre door, Dressing-table, enclosed with larger drawers, the top fitted with large swing mirror and jewel drawers, Washstand. with Carrara marble slab and Mintoa tile back, with shaving glass, the bottom prettily enclosed with cupboard and drawers, Chairs. and Towel Rail com- plete ; a very pretty suite. What price for this, £25 or £3O ? No, only 9 guineas. Money returned if not satisfactory. Ten per cent extra if credit is given. W. 11. WOESLEY, "The Pantheon," Gaythorn, Manchester. See Advertisement on page 4.</p>
