      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-06-23_WidnesExaminer_art0029" n="art0029">
        <head>IS IT TRUE?</head>
        <p>IS IT TRUE?</p>
        <p>We are used to "tall yarns" from" Yankee-land and in fact, can hardly pick up an American newspapel Without seeing an article referring to some new improb- able invention; a recent discovery, or some wonderful feat,which,if true, would command our wonder,astonish- ment and praise. While we could not reflect upon the veracity of our American cousins, we must in all con- science, and in justice to ourselves and readers, accept many of these statements with a grain or two of allow- ance, even if we credit their incongruity to inaccuracy Of cables or typographical errors. When we receive a startling statement, however, of facts occurinn• or a dis- covery made, in England, verified by one of our own countrymen of professional and social standing, we have no hesitancy in accepting it as" true." The latest and one of the most interesting experiments is reported and Was made by Prof. J. Poiraud, 8.5. C.. of "The Nut- -3e11,” Wargrave, Henley-on-Thames, and his report is Worthy the careful attention of the public. He says : " Weeks of treatment by the best London Physicans failed to relieve or cure me of Inflammation of the Bladder and Prostate gland, but Warner's Safe Cure cured me, and now I Can conscientiously say that my Present good health is solely attributable to this scienti- fic preparation."</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON TECITNICAL INSTITUTE.</p>
        <p>The results of the examinations held under the Union of Lancashire and Cheshire Institutes are llovr to hand, and we give below the names of the successful candidates. CONTINUATION SCHOOL. ENGLISH (ELEMENTARY),ISt class : Carpenter,Mary J.; Parker, W. 2nd class : Greene, H. ; liorobin, Sarah E. ; London, Bertha C.; Lcndon, Ella C.; Longshaw, T. ; McGarty, Florence ; Penney,Susannah. ARITHMETIC (ELEM,NTARY), Ist class : Baines, W. R. Carpenter, Mary J. ; Cooper, H.C. ; Gandy, T. ; Haigh, R• G. ; Longshaw, T. ; McGarty, Francis J. ; Summer- field, E. 2nd class: Barton' J. ; Basketter, Annie G. ; %dim. Pranci; Chadwick, J. ; Gandy, M. ; Greene, 11. ; Gill, Edith ; Hawthorn, J. L. ; Hill, J. ; Harding,T. H. ; Horobin, Sitah E. ; L mdon, Bertha; London, Ella ; Looker,J. ; McGarty,Florence ; Parker,W. ; Penney, 11.3annah. NEEDLEWORK, ISt class with distinction: Gill, Edith ; Horobiu, Sarah E.; Warburton, Edith B. Ist class: Basketter, Annie Cr. ; Penny, Susannah. 2nd class: Prior, ' Catherine. COOKERY, 2nd class: Gill, Edith; McGarty, Florence; 3rd class: Chadwick, Esther.</p>
