        <p>Bens's COCOLINE.--Cocoa-Nib Extract. (Tea-like).—The choicest roast,d nibs (broken up be ins) of the natural Cocoa, on being subjected to powerful hydraulic pressure, give forth their excess of oil, lesying for use a finely-flavoured powder— " Cocoaine," a product which, when prepared with boiling water, has the consistence of tea, of which it is now bene- fieially taking the place with n,any. its active principle being a gewle nerve stimulant. supplies the needed energy without unduly exciting the system. Sold only in packets and tins, by drocers. labelled "James Epps and Co. Ltd., Homceopathic Chemists, London," To he obtainel in Wa rington of BOWDEN and SONS, Sankey-street ; BAMFORD, 132, Bridge-street, : PEacwAr„ 14 Buttermarket-street ; IlierrAttnsoN and SON, Bridge-street ; and others in every town,—Adrt.</p>
