        <p>FAIRFIELD V. CEMETERY WHITE ROSE.—This match was played on Saturday on the ground of the former. Scores :—Fairfield, 28 ; Cemetery 15. TRINITY 2ND V. BEWSF.Y WESLEYANS 2ND.—This match was played on the Wesleyan ground, the visitors winning an easy game by 69 runs. Score :—lrinity 2nd 91 ; Weskyans 2ad, 22. FRIEND'S SCHOOL, PENRETH, V. SANREY WIRE MILLS. —ln glorious weather this match was played at Lovely- lane, on Saturday. The wire mills won the toss and sent the, School in to hat. They were not disposed of ! until 96 were reached. Reynolds making 54 in fine style. ! Williams with his 10b3, was most effective towards the close of the innings of the Wire Mills. Marshall was the only ono who suffered any serious resistance, and he played steadily for his runs. Woodcock made one or two good hits. The game was finished two minutes .before time, leaving the School again victors, this time by 32 runs. Scores :—Penketh f. 46, Sankey 64.</p>
        <p>LYISIBI GRAMMAR SCHOOL V. BROOSLANDS SCHOOL.— Played at Brooklands on Saturday. The game resulted in a victory for the visitors by eight wickets. Score : 13rooklands School, 32 and 30 ; Lymm Grammar School, 32 and 31 (for 2 wicket). ARPLEY JUNIORS V. PENRETH FRIEND'S SCHOOL 2ND.— This match was °laved at Sankey and resulted in a win for thehome team by 19 runs. Score :—Arpley Juniors, 21; Penketh, 40. WARRINGTON V. SEFTON.—ThiS match was played at Warrington, and resulted in a win for Warrrington. Scores and bowling analysis :</p>
