      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-06-23_WidnesExaminer_art0107" n="art0107">
        <head>SHADOW OF WAR.</head>
        <p>THE SHADOW OF WAR.</p>
        <p>The "World "concludes an alarmfgt article under the above heading as follows :—ln plain English, a French invasion is no chimera; no mere bugbear or bogey to frighten children, but under certain conditions a very real, tangible, and feasible undertaking. The " silver streak " is no longer a natural barrier ; it can be too I easily bridged in these days of steam. Transport would of course, be required, but there is more than enough in French harbours to fern, across a formidable army of a hundred or two hundred thousand men, and that army ; could be concentrated with ease and rapidity on the French littoral. In such a case we may be allowed to hope that time will be an important factor among Eng- land's chances, as at least a couple of days would be required to complete the landing, even if it were unop- posed on shore, during which the British fleet would hardly remain an idle or indifferent spectator of the descent. But although deemed generally superior to the best naval force that might be employed to cover the landing, our Channel fleet is not overwhelmingly so, and fleets before have been fought, evaded, or held at bay, There would be the last resource, a struggle on the soil of our country, and pride forbids us to contemplate reverse when fighting with our backs to the wall. Even the final expulsion of the invaders would be a sorry set- off to the paralysis of industry, the losses, the ruined homes, the general havoc that would overwhelm the country, and the terrible insult offered to our hitherto inviolate land. The picture is not pleasant, but in the present temper of an excitable nation like our French neighbour such trials are by no means remote or impos- sible, and there is but too much reason to suppose that the tense character of the situation is very seriously occupying the attention of the British Government. YOUR ATTENTION PLEASE!</p>
