      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-06-23_WidnesExaminer_art0138" n="art0138">
        <head>EMPLOYERS AND WORKMEN IN FRANCE</head>
        <p>EMPLOYERS AND WORKMEN IN FRANCE</p>
        <p>EXTRAORDINARY COMPENSATION PROPOSALS. ' The " Daily Chronicle " Paris correspondent tßle- graPhs :—The law of compensation by employers to the surviving families of workmen killed while in their employ is about to encounter a new form of resistance. One filth of the deceased workman's wages would, in c4Ee of live orphans, make the manufacturer liable for the whole sum earned, and would have to he pald miii the sixteenth year of each recipient. With the presneet of such legislation toasters will decline to employ work- men with children. French medical men argue th it this course, if adopted, will increase the serious depQpu- lation now going on in France.</p>
