        <p>FURNISH at WORSLEY'S, GAYTHORN. HIGH-CLASS SECOND-HAND FURNITURE, THE PANTHEON, GAYTHORN, MANCHESTER. WEEKLY CHAT.—The great advantage of Second-hand Furniture over new lies in the fact that it has borne the test proving its stability. The world's desire to have everything at the lowest possible price, together with the enormous competition, the introduction of steatn power, has all tended to the production of cheap new jerry furniture. ut erly regardless of the one essential in furniture—stability. Worsley's warn the public against purchasing new London Furniture, when furniture by Lamb. Gillows, Ogden, Starkey,' and Neild, Garnett, Sze.. may be had for half the price of the New London Rubbish sold so largely by drapers. As an example, we have a Magnificent Sideboard, 7 feet long, by Henry Ogden and Sons. cost originally £BO, is in splendid condition ; our price £l5. What a farce to purchase new when the second-hand is so much superior in make and finish. Worsley's have nearly 100 Second-hand Sideboards in stock by all the best known makers of the day, from 355. to £5O. To ‘prove the disadvantages of new London fwniture, we were asked to buy a set of Drawing-room Furniture which had cost £4B, this had only been in wear a little over twelve months, yet we found it impossible to give £lO for it, the fact being it was worthless, we advised it being sold by auction. Worsley's guarantee every article sold for at least five years, all the heavy articles for a lifetime, and we claim that by combining the advantages of second-hand with the requisite and necessary portion of our new stock, which is All our own make, that we can completely put all competition in the shade. All we ask is the favour of a visit, and as e will quickly demonstrate the truth of these assertions. Far away the largest stock in the North. Inspt•ction freely invited. You are not expected to buy. The same courtesy shown to those looking round as to those purchasing. Established 1841.</p>
